## Two modes (steal this split; do not add a library)

Open-source grids (Handsontable keyboard contexts, Luckysheet/Univer editor overlay, WAI-ARIA APG **grid** + roving tabindex) all split:

| Mode | Look | Keys |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Selected** | Focus ring on the display cell (`#007AFF` / `--ok-blue`). No caret. `tabIndex=0` on the active cell, `-1` on others | Arrows move **cell**. Tab / Shift+Tab move cell (wrap to next/prev row). Enter / F2 **begin insert-edit**. Printable **begin overwrite-edit**. Delete / Backspace **clear** to `null`. Ctrl/Cmd+C copies the committed display string (not `"—"` → copy `""`). Ctrl/Cmd+V overwrite-edits then commits on the usual commit keys (or commit immediately on paste — pick one and test). |
| **Editing** | The `<input>` is focused | Arrows / Home / End move **caret only**, including at string edges — **never** commit-and-move (Sheets-accurate; Excel “Enter mode” is **dropped**). Enter commits + move **down** into selected. Shift+Enter commits + **up**. Tab commits + **right** (wrap). Shift+Tab commits + **left**. Escape cancels. Delete/Backspace edit the string. |

After commit+move, the destination is **selected**, not editing.

**Click:**

- Click a different editable cell: if editing, **commit** current, **select** the target (do not auto-edit the target).
- Click already-selected: start insert-edit.
- Double-click: insert-edit.
- Click non-cell (sidebar, another control): commit if editing.

**Edges:** arrows at first/last cell **stay**. Tab from last cell of last row stays (or wrap within the lift — stay is Sheets-like for sheet edge). Do not create sets by navigating off the bottom.

**preventDefault** on Tab / Arrows / Enter when the grid owns focus so focus does not escape to the browser chrome.

